Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: pngset.c
Line: 794
Function: png_set_PLTE
Bug type: heap-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-122
Explanation: When info_ptr->color_type is PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE, num_palette is validated against (1 << info_ptr->bit_depth) (lines 751-765), but the allocation for png_ptr->palette is always for PNG_MAX_PALETTE_LENGTH entries (256) (lines 790-791). If info_ptr->bit_depth is erroneously > 8, the check can permit num_palette > 256, leading to memcpy copying num_palette entries into a buffer sized for only 256 entries (lines 793-795), causing a heap buffer overflow.

Source context:
